				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Add inline workspace folders to extension host init data\n\nAdd `folders` array directly to the WorkspaceDTO in InitData so extensions that read `vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders` synchronously in their `activate()` (vscode.git, eamodio.gitlens, typescript) see the real folders immediately instead of `[]` until a delta fires. Cocoon's `WorkspaceNamespace/Index.ts` reads this at shim construction time, so the folders must be present in the initial payload.\n\nAlso add `configuration` field to pass the workspace config path, and change CWD-autoload default to ON in debug builds (OFF in release). Debug builds need folders for `vscode.git` / `eamodio.gitlens` to scan repositories and surface tree-views, while release keeps the stock VS Code UX. Override with `LAND_AUTOLOAD_CWD=0` or `=1`.",
			"SHA": "e10a5c042b7f00b9a5e984f84d3ac65bf32de5d9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T00:09:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add child-exit detection to Cocoon gRPC and activation-race command handling\n\nTwo related reliability improvements for Mountain-to-Cocoon communication:\n\n1. **CommandProvider.rs**: Handle TOCTOU race where TypeScript extension's post-activation pipeline invokes `_typescript.configurePlugin` within the same event-loop tick as its own `registerCommand`. The intervening executeCommand finds no handler and emits alarming red errors. Add early return with null for internal-underscore-prefixed commands (`_typescript.*`, `_extensionHost.*`, `_workbench.registerWebview*`) that the extension expects to be safely droppable if the registry hasn't caught up yet. The extension's own try/catch takes the expected \"not yet available\" path.\n\n2. **CocoonManagement.rs**: Add child-exit detection during the gRPC connection loop. Before each retry, poll `ChildProcess.try_wait()` to detect if Node has already died. If exited, abandon the loop immediately with the exit status embedded in the error (1 = unhandled exception, 13 = invalid module) instead of continuing to retry against a dead process. Also add explicit error messages that point developers at the real failure (missing bundle, ESM/CJS import drift) rather than abstract \"connection refused\" messages.\n\nThese changes complete the exponential backoff work from the previous commit by ensuring Mountain fails fast with actionable diagnostics when Cocoon spawns but immediately exits.",
			"SHA": "26891b3039a723a3a410e073c4d00ec4064b8834"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T00:09:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				872,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Implement exponential backoff for Cocoon gRPC handshake\n\nReplace the fixed 1-second retry poll in Mountain-to-Cocoon gRPC connection with exponential backoff (50ms initial, 2s ceiling, 20s budget). The previous approach wasted 18 seconds waiting after Cocoon's ~200ms bind completion on successful startups, while still taking a full 20s to detect genuine failures.\n\nAlso add comprehensive documentation for the `dual-track` tag in DevLog.rs, which logs progressive Rust migration dispatch decisions (mountain, node-fallback, unavailable, error) to surface the VS Code API coverage gap as a searchable TODO list.\n\nAdd a pre-flight bundle probe constant to fail fast with an actionable error when the Cocoon bundle is missing (esbuild failure, incomplete checkout) instead of spawning Node into a dying require() chain.\n\nImpact: Healthy spawns now connect in ~400ms (attempts 3-5) vs previous ~20s; failure detection still triggers at the 20s budget.",
			"SHA": "115a48df9dbdbad30a28fa4a99d27c0557565ee4"
		}
	],
